  "prefLabel": "Env-A 103.42 Heat release",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 103.42 “Heat release” means the amount of heat liberated by the complete combustion of a given unit of specific material from the inside volume of the furnace in which the combustion takes place, expressed as calories per second per cubic meter or BTUs per hour per cubic foot.\n\nSource. #1717, eff 2-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss and moved by #5033, eff 12-27-90 (see Env-A 101.48)\n\nNew. #5033, eff 12-27-90 (from Env-A 101.46); ss and moved by #6057-A, eff 6-30-95 (from Env-A 101.47); renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.145), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304, (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.96), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.98) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html"
